    "created_at": "2025-01-02T16:21:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-02T16:21:17Z",
    "body": "The OpenAPI (Swagger) syntax is only one of several syntaxes already prevalent in the ecosystem. The syntax that was chosen was based on the popular path-to-regexp library, and is similar to, for example, the Ruby on Rails router syntax, among others. There are also concepts that are possible to express in the current syntax that I don't believe are expressible in the Swagger syntax, though I haven't dug in more detail.\r\n\r\nThe bottom line here, though, is that it's probably too late to make such a change in this case, as it would be backward incompatible and at least one engine (Chromium) has been shipping this syntax for some time.",
