    "updated_at": "2025-01-03T05:33:02Z",
    "body": "That's unfortunate, and I would like to voice my criticism for that decision and going forward on it. :/ Because OpenAPI has/is a specification and is considered a standard spanning multiple ecosystems. A popular library in one ecosystem doesn't really define a standard outside their corresponding ecosystem (rails, express, etc.). Now another standard has been created, and we are again in the world of said XKCD comic strip. :(",
